":1520,"dbpm":-0.1,"adjd":108.7,"stl":1.2,"blk":0.1,"drb":10.1,"pf":1.7},{"name":"Damari Wheeler-Thomas","team":"North Dakota St. (ref)","role":"Combo G","minPct":69,"score":28.3,"rank":1637,"v1rank":1855,"drapm":-0.87,"rapmPoss":1661,"dbpm":-1.5,"adjd":110.5,"stl":2,"blk":0,"drb":10.2,"pf":3.4,"isRef":1}]},"notes":["<b style=\"color:var(--text)\">How RAPM was built.</b> 6,027 games passed a whole-game minutes check (every player within 2.5 min of the box; 248 failed). They produced <b style=\"color:var(--text)\">213,740 lineup stints</b> for 8,888 players. Each stint gets one row per side: points scored ~ the 5 offensive players + the 5 defenders, weighted by possessions. Solved with ridge regression (conjugate gradient) for 17,776 offensive and defensive ratings. Shown for players with 300+ possessions (3,541).","<b style=\"color:var(--text)\">Shrinkage chosen on held-out games.</b> I hid 10% of games, fit on the rest, and scored predictions on the hidden games. Two different folds both peaked at λ ≈ 600–1,000, so the final fit uses <b style=\"color:var(--text)\">λ = 700</b>. Spread among 1,500+ possession players: ORAPM ±2.6, DRAPM ±2.7 pts/100 (1 SD). The DEF score swaps shrunk on/off for DRAPM at the same 20% weight.","<b style=\"color:var(--text)\">Eye test: v1 → v2.</b><br>• <b style=\"color:var(--text)\">Fixed:</b> Maliq Brown #46 → #23 and Monroe #7 → #15. RAPM separates them from their teammates.<br>• <b style=\"color:var(--text)\">Box score as a check:</b> Loyer has an elite +8.7 DRAPM but weak box numbers, so his DEF is 84, not 99. The blend tempers RAPM outliers.<br>• <b style=\"color:var(--text)\">Watch:</b> Boozer is back to #10 (from #34), and the top-50 halo count went 9 → 12. Ridge RAPM pulls everyone toward zero, so the starters on elite defenses soak up team credit. The fix is a <b style=\"color:var(--text)\">box-score-prior RAPM</b> (shrink toward DBPM instead of 0) plus a prior season."]}